<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pridi Banomyong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1900">1900</a>–<a href="/years/1983">1983</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pridi Banomyong was a Thai lawyer and statesman, a leader of the civilian wing of the People's Party that ended absolute monarchy in 1932. He drafted early constitutions, founded Thammasat University and led the Free Thai movement against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Briefly prime minister in 1946, he was forced into exile after the death of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ananda-mahidol">Ananda Mahidol</a> and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pridi-banomyong.jpg" alt="Pridi Banomyong" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thai government (รัฐบาลไทย) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pridi_Banomyong_in_Uniform_Photo_1946.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
